-- title:
--   Descent of a modular function and a residue value to a number field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, let $k$ be a field and $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ a ring homomorphism, let $a \in k$ lie in the range of $\mathrm{red}$, and let $f$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, that is of the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the image, under the coefficient embedding of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ into Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, of the subfield `modularFunctionFieldFull (1 * q)` of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb{Q})$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the divisor expansions of level $1 \cdot q$. Then there is an intermediate field $K$ of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, such that: (i) the Laurent series underlying $f$ lies in `NodeLocalized.fieldOver (1 * q) K`, the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ generated by the constant series attached to elements of $K$ together with the two series `jqModC` and `jqNModC` of level $1 \cdot q$; and (ii) there is an element $x$ of `NodeLocalized.coeffSubring A K`, the intersection $A \cap K$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, whose image under $\mathrm{red}$ (restricted along the inclusion $A \cap K \subseteq A$) equals $a$. Thus a single number field $K$ serves simultaneously for a presentation of $f$ over $K$ and for a lift of $a$ in $A \cap K$.
--
--   This is the descent step that replaces the coefficient field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by a number field: it produces one finite extension $K/\mathbb{Q}$ over which a given level-$q$ modular function is expressible in $j$ and $j_q$ and over which a prescribed residue in $k$ is already attained. It is used in the node-localisation and Deligne–Rapoport model constructions for $X_0(q)$, where arguments must be carried out over a number field with an integral structure at the chosen valuation.
